# Publish the site from main. Continuous: every merge is a release. No version numbers,
# no qualification step; the check on the pull request was the proof.
# Levels come from the `verification-results` branch the verify workflow writes (OSD-D5).
name: pages
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  workflow_dispatch:
permissions: { contents: read, pages: write, id-token: write }
concurrency: { group: pages, cancel-in-progress: true }
jobs:
  publish:
    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04
    timeout-minutes: 10
    environment: { name: github-pages, url: "${{ steps.deploy.outputs.page_url }}" }
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with: { fetch-depth: 0 }
      - uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@v3
        with: { python-version: "3.12" }
      - run: uv sync
      - name: latest verification results
        run: |
          if git ls-remote --exit-code origin verification-results >/dev/null; then
            git fetch -q origin verification-results
            mkdir -p build/verification
            git archive origin/verification-results | tar -x -C build/verification
          fi
      - name: tippecanoe 2.49.0 (Ubuntu 24.04 package, pinned by hash; E15 tiles)
        run: |
          curl -fsSLo /tmp/tippecanoe.deb http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/universe/t/tippecanoe/tippecanoe_2.49.0-1build1_amd64.deb
          echo "0ab1c2f65e9f836b9097de0864de32016f4a8e0226ed10822c7eb12391983308  /tmp/tippecanoe.deb" | sha256sum -c
          sudo dpkg -i /tmp/tippecanoe.deb && tippecanoe --version
      - run: make build
      - uses: actions/configure-pages@v5
      - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3
        with: { path: site }
      - id: deploy
        uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4
     1	## E09 Ophiolite reads the catalogue — QUEUED · Kernel, cross-repo · strategy at lane open · one Codex round
     2	
     3	Authority: owner direction 23 Oct ("verified bits … pull into their workspace"); Ophiolite E85
     4	(one intake), E35 (rights-basis), E55 (kind registry), E122 (provenance).
     5	
     6	**Outcome.** In an Ophiolite project a person pastes a manifest or STAC collection address into
     7	the intake, the files land through the normal upload run, every landed item carries a
     8	rights-basis filled from the record's licence, and the fidelity record says which files converted
     9	to which canonical type and which did not. That is level L4.
    10	
    11	**Context today (verified 23 Oct for this repository; Ophiolite side from program memory, to be
    12	re-verified at lane open).** Ophiolite's E85 intake accepts "an address" as a drop; E35
    13	rights-basis/1 exists on uploads; E57 reads LAS 1.2/3.0 and DLIS; E123 reads ZGY. The Ophiolite
    14	monorepo is private; this repository's reader interface is `osd.manifest.read` (E06). Ophiolite
    15	ships an NLOG sample in its try-it image (E79).
    16	
    17	**The design the lane must map to.**
    18	1. Two halves, two repositories, one interface: here, the manifest and STAC are the contract and
    19	   gain nothing Ophiolite-specific; there, an intake address handler recognises `osd.manifest/1`
    20	   and STAC collections.
    21	2. Rights: `licence.{name, spdx, url, statement, share_alike}` map to Ophiolite's rights-basis
    22	   fields; `redistribution: unknown` becomes the rights-basis state that refuses publication
    23	   (E35's refusal state) while allowing private use.
    24	3. Fidelity record: written by the Ophiolite run, exported back as `verification` check
    25	   `canonical-conversion` with detail "<n> of <m> files to <kinds>", so this repository's
    26	   verifier can read it from a file the Ophiolite run publishes (no live coupling).
    27	4. Provenance: each landed item's E122 record names the catalogue item id and the catalogue
    28	   version (git commit of this repository at build time, written into `records.json`).
    29	5. The NLOG sample in E79 and the `nlog/nlog` record agree on kinds and licence text.
    30	
    31	**Acceptance.**
    32	- Here: `records.json` carries `catalog_version` (commit); a manifest fixture round-trips through
    33	  `osd.manifest.read` with every licence field intact (test).
